/; FW_GC_STRESS
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/; A brought file's top-level `spawn` must still be drained.
/;
/; Brought top-level code is emitted into __fw_brought_init_<i>, which main
/; calls before running its own statements. The drain call is emitted ONLY in
/; main (IRGenerator.cpp, just before handleReturn), never in the brought-init
/; function — so a task queued by the library depends entirely on main's drain
/; to run at all.
/;
/; Ordering below pins that down: library top-level, then main's body, then the
/; library's task — because the task waits for main's drain, not the library's
/; own initialisation.
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
bring "spawn_support/spawn_toplevel_lib.fg"

println("main")
